-- title:
--   Inertia fixes the prime-to-p toric points at level Γ_H(M)
-- statement:
--   Fix natural numbers $p$ and $M$ with $p$ prime and $M \neq 0$, a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$, and a divisibility $p \mid M$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` satisfying `A.LiesOverPrime p`, i.e. $p$ lies in the nonunits of $A$, and assume its residue field has characteristic $p$ and is algebraically closed. Let $\Lambda$ be level data of type `JHNeronObjectAtP.LevelData p M H hpM A` — a structure comprising a morphism $\sigma_A$ from $\operatorname{Spec} A$ to the base scheme `base p` compatible with the generic point, a scheme $X$ over `base p` with a relative group law, and bijections of its generic-fibre sections with $J_H(M/p)$ at the induced level and of its sections over the residue point with the degree-zero divisor class group $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the reduction — and let $O$ be a Néron object `JHNeronObjectAtP p M H hpM A hA Λ`. Let $m$ be a natural number coprime to $p$. The assertion is: for every $\sigma$ in `A.inertiaSubgroupIn ℚ`, the image in $\operatorname{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ of the inertia subgroup of the decomposition subgroup of $A$, and for every $y$ in `O.toricPts m` — the subgroup of $J_H(M,H)$ generated by the range of `O.toricPoint m` when $m > 0$, and the trivial subgroup otherwise — one has $\sigma \cdot y = y$.
--
--   This records that the prime-to-$p$ part of the toric contribution to the points of the Néron object of $J_H(M)$ at a place above $p$ is unramified: the toric points coming from $\mu_m$ with $p \nmid m$ are inertia-invariant. It feeds the monodromy and displacement estimates for the toric part, and is cited in the construction of elements with prescribed $(\sigma - 1)$-behaviour in [`ModularCurve.JHNeronObjectAtP.exists_forall_mem_toricPts_exists_smul_sub_eq_of_coprime_of_abelJacobiPin_of_atkinLehner`](thm.html#ModularCurve.JHNeronObjectAtP.exists_forall_mem_toricPts_exists_smul_sub_eq_of_coprime_of_abelJacobiPin_of_atkinLehner).
